@startuml

title The run grant

hide empty description

[*] --> active : iam.v1.run_grants.put\n(the grantor holds every\npermission of the grant's role)

active : each exchange checks the audience,\nthe tenant and the grantor

active --> revoked : iam.v1.ops.revoke_run_grant\n(unschedule, delete,\nchange of party)
active --> exhausted : a manual grant\nreaches max_runs
active --> expired : not_after passes
revoked --> [*]
exhausted --> [*]
expired --> [*]

note right of active
  An exchange answers forbidden, grant_lapsed,
  when the grantor is inactive or no longer holds
  the permissions in the party. Lapse is a check at
  exchange, not a stored state: the grant stays
  active until its owning service revokes it.
end note

@enduml
